v_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":61.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.19747478981206049,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.1365973895329815,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":68.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.1759280128172612,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":92.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08914709804887999,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":69.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.6389068378815139,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.010878918679790517,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":60.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0.21659738953298152,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.007413852711029678,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":40.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.06688533564966166,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.013990001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alkermes plc, a biopharmaceutical company, engages in the research, development, and commercialization of pharmaceutical products to address unmet medical needs of patients in therapeutic areas in the United States, Ireland, and internationally. The company has a portfolio of proprietary commercial products for the treatment of opioid dependence, alcohol dependence, schizophrenia, bipolar I, and a pipeline of clinical and preclinical product candidates in development for neurological disorders. Its marketed products include ARISTADA, an intramuscular injectable suspension for the treatment of schizophrenia; ARISTADA INITIO for the treatment of schizophrenia in adults; VIVITROL for the treatment of alcohol and prevention of opioid dependence; LYBALVI, an oral atypical antipsychotic drug candidate for the treatment of adults with schizophrenia and bipolar I disorder; and LUMRYZ, an extended-release oral suspension product for the treatment of cataplexy or EDS in pediatric patients. The company also offers proprietary technology platforms to third parties to enable them to develop, commercialize, and manufacture products. It has collaboration agreements primarily with Janssen Pharmaceutica N.V., Janssen Pharmaceutica Inc, and Janssen Pharmaceutica International. Alkermes plc was founded in 1987 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Blair C. Jackson | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $720K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $234K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Alkermes plc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.9B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +3.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $480M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 21\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 85% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.853017438375392},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 22% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Clinical Data Wave Might Change The Case For Investing In Alkermes Stock (ALKS)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-alks/alkermes/news/clinical-data-wave-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-al","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486798.222,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alkermes plc $ALKS Shares Newly Acquired by M&G PLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/alkermes-plc-alks-shares-newly-acquired-by-mg-plc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794392763.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of ALKS and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Behavioral_Patterns_of_ALKS_and_Institutional_Flows_110926081402_1794273242.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794273242.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Did Alkermes (ALKS) Shares Climb After Its Latest Update?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-alks/alkermes/news/why-did-alkermes-alks-shares-climb-after-its-latest-update","